<%# The birthday / age-gate lab page.

    WHAT ONLY A BROWSER CAN SEE HERE. The server's bytes are identical whether
    the handoff works: both cards render, both carry their CTAs, and every
    String assertion in test/views passes either way. What the markup cannot
    contain is the PROGRAM — birthdayModal's submit(), which decides that an
    under-age date is a refusal rather than an error and swaps one card for
    another on the store. Until 2026-08-24 that path did not exist; the card
    turned red and disabled its own button, and the tests that "covered" it were
    asserting on text that was present in both states.

    The lab sets up LOCALS and nothing else. Both cards are the engine's own
    partials rendered by name; the page reimplements neither, or the spec would
    be grading the lab. demo: true keeps it off the network — there is no
    /age/verify in the dummy, and inventing one would test the fiction rather
    than the handoff. demo_underage is what steers the local resolve down the
    refused branch, which is the whole subject of the spec.

    Two hosts' worth of ids on ONE store, because the handoff crosses them: the
    birthday card swaps to 'age-gate', so both must be registered or the swap
    lands on an id nothing renders and the modal goes blank. That blankness is
    itself a defect this page can catch. %>
<main class="p-8" x-data>
  <p data-test="lab-body">birthday gate lab</p>

  <%# The factory, at PAGE level — not inside the host below. A <script> cloned
      out of an Alpine <template> never runs, which is why the engine homes
      birthdayModal in its own partial and asks every consumer to render it once
      in the layout. Omitting it is silent: x-data="birthdayModal(...)" throws,
      the component never mounts, and the card renders as an empty shell with no
      DOB selects and no submit button. This lab page shipped without it for one
      run, and the browser lane is what said so — every server-side assertion
      about that same card was green at the time. %>
  <%= render "studio/birthday_assets" %>

  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mb-6">
    <%# Opens the card down the PASSING branch — submit resolves to success. %>
    <button type="button" data-test="open-birthday"
            class="btn btn-primary"
            @click="$store.labModals.open('birthday', {})">
      Open birthday
    </button>

    <%# The refused branch. demo_underage is a server-side LOCAL, not a prop, so
        this is a second registration of the SAME partial rather than a prop on
        the first — the style guide reaches the same place through a wrapper that
        reads props; the lab takes the shorter road. %>
    <button type="button" data-test="open-birthday-underage"
            class="btn btn-outline"
            @click="$store.labModals.open('birthday-underage', {})">
      Open birthday (underage)
    </button>

    <%# The refusal card on its own, for the assertions that do not need the
        handoff to have run. %>
    <button type="button" data-test="open-age-gate"
            class="btn btn-outline"
            @click="$store.labModals.open('age-gate', { minAge: 21, state: 'CA' })">
      Open age gate
    </button>
  </div>

  <%= render "studio/modals/scoped_host", store: "labModals" do %>
    <template x-if="$store.labModals.current().id === 'birthday'">
      <div><%= render "studio/modals/blocks/birthday",
            min_age:       21,
            state:         "CA",
            submit_url:    "#lab-birthday",
            modal_store:   "labModals",
            demo:          true,
            demo_underage: false,
            fine_print:    "Lab policy: 21+ in CA." %></div>
    </template>

    <%# The refused twin. Same partial, demo_underage flipped — the id is chosen
        by the opener's prop, which the two templates below read. %>
    <template x-if="$store.labModals.current().id === 'birthday-underage'">
      <div><%= render "studio/modals/blocks/birthday",
            min_age:       21,
            state:         "CA",
            submit_url:    "#lab-birthday",
            modal_store:   "labModals",
            demo:          true,
            demo_underage: true,
            fine_print:    "Lab policy: 21+ in CA." %></div>
    </template>

    <template x-if="$store.labModals.current().id === 'age-gate'">
      <div><%= render "studio/modals/blocks/age_gate",
            min_age:           21,
            state:             "CA",
            watch_url:         "/lab/birthday_gate?watched=1",
            birthday_modal_id: "birthday",
            modal_store:       "labModals" %></div>
    </template>
  <% end %>
</main>
